Chapter: ThemeInkOnTest

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites UI chapter Theme

 WORKS-17. An ink that is legible on a given ground, per scheme.

 The arms are paired against the two ways this can be wrong. A helper that
 IGNORED the ground would answer the same ink for black and for white, so
 every palette is asked both and the two answers must differ: that pair is
 the falsifying arm and it needs no pixels. And a helper that answered some
 fixed colour rather than one of the palette's own would drift out of the
 scheme, so each answer is printed beside that palette's two text colours.

 The luminance is printed rather than the verdict, because "legible" is the
 claim and a number on either side of the midpoint is what supports it. A
 dark ground must take a light ink and a light ground a dark one, and the
 midpoint is 127.

Section: Fixtures

  black : Integer = 0

  white : Integer = 16777215

  named : Integer -> Text
  named (i) =
    if i == 0 then "terminal" else if i == 1 then "lcars" else "minimal"

  pal-of : Integer -> Palette
  pal-of (i) =
    if i == 0 then palette-terminal else if i == 1 then palette-lcars else palette-minimal

Section: Reporting

  report : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  report (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then print-line-uni ""
    else act
      let p = pal-of i
      in let acc = p.pal-accent
      in print-line-uni (named i & ": bg luma " & show (theme-luma (p.pal-bg)) & ", fg luma " & show (theme-luma (p.pal-fg)) & ", accent luma " & show (theme-luma acc) & " -> ink luma " & show (theme-luma (theme-ink-on p acc)))
      report (i + 1) n
    end

  flips : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  flips (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then print-line-uni ""
    else act
      let p = pal-of i
      in let on-black = theme-ink-on p black
      in let on-white = theme-ink-on p white
      in print-line-uni ("  " & named i & ": on black luma " & show (theme-luma on-black) & ", on white luma " & show (theme-luma on-white) & (if on-black == on-white then "   SAME, the ground is being ignored" else ""))
      flips (i + 1) n
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni "the ink each scheme puts on its own accent:"
    report 0 3
    print-line-uni "the same helper asked for black and for white:"
    flips 0 3
  end
